pve-compose (0.0.3-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * The compose file and the facts file inside the guest go through the
    guest-files library (manifest-tracked, atomic, refused by name when
    another writer recorded the path) instead of a bare pct push.
    Comment-key stripping is gone with it: the server strips notes.

 -- Julius Arkenberg <julius@rkenberg.de>  Mon, 21 Sep 2026 19:45:00 +0200

pve-compose (0.0.2-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * The stack directory lives on the rootfs; there is no stack disk. Only
    x-pve volumes get disks of their own. `stack.storage`, `stack.size` and
    `stack.project` are gone from the document (the project is the hostname).
  * No built-in storage guess. `new` takes the template and disk storages
    from a flag, the persisted config, or a question at the terminal, and
    offers to store an answer; every question is asked before anything is
    done. An x-pve disk without a storage on a node without a stored one is
    refused with the command that fixes it.
  * `pve-compose config [set|unset <key> [value]]` shows and changes the
    persisted choices; the file needs no hand editing.
  * Removed: `pct template`, `apply --reboot`, `new --stack-size`, the
    cluster-wide storage default, `nodes.<n>.bridge`, `defaults.swap`.

 -- Julius Arkenberg <julius@rkenberg.de>  Mon, 14 Sep 2026 16:30:00 +0200

pve-compose (0.0.1-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * First version. One docker compose stack per LXC wrapper, described by the
    `compose` subtree of the guest's pve-meta document.
  * Verbs: new, apply, diff, status, upgrade; `pct` and `docker` halves of each;
    unknown `docker` verbs pass through to docker compose in /opt/stack.
  * No migrate verb: moving a stack to a new wrapper is a documented manual
    recipe (README, "Migrating a stack by hand"; docs/ROADMAP.md).
  * Per-node reconcile loop (systemd unit) driven by pve-meta's version token;
    applies document changes to running stacks, never starts a stack.
  * Named compose volumes become PVE mountpoint disks or host binds via x-pve,
    identified by mount path, grow-only, never deleted.
  * Docker installed from get.docker.com into the upstream Debian template;
    no prebuilt template.
  * Ships the `compose` pve-meta prefix; the selector's tag is the tag it
    watches.

 -- Julius Arkenberg <julius@rkenberg.de>  Mon, 14 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
